# Keep the build context small. Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored —
# reproducible Docker builds need it.
target/
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.fleet/
.env
.env.example
.DS_Store
README.md
CLAUDE.md
docker-compose.yml
# Railway IaC authoring (.railway/railway.ts) and its npm toolchain. Nothing on
# the Railway side ever reads this file — the CLI does, from a workstation
# working tree — so it has no business in the build context. Keeping
# node_modules out matters too: both COPY . . stages would otherwise bust the
# cargo-chef layer on every edit.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
.railway/
# The frozen v1 contract and its lint config are build ARTIFACTS: the Explorer
# generates its client from them, Prism bind-mounts them from the host, and CI
# lints them from the checkout. Nothing in either image reads them, and leaving
# them in the context would bust the builder's `COPY . .` on every spec edit.
openapi/
